<title>GERMANY: GRUNDIG 1996 LOSS NARROWS TO 553 MLN DM.</title>
<headline>GRUNDIG 1996 LOSS NARROWS TO 553 MLN DM.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996:</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net loss			     553     vs 598</p>
<p>    Group operating loss		     382     vs 288</p>
<p>    Group sales				  3,320   vs 3,500</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German consumer electronics group is</p>
<p>Grundig AG [GRNG.CN]. The 1996 business year is the last in</p>
<p>which the company's largest shareholder, Philips , is</p>
<p>required to compensate Grundig losses.</p>
<p>Christian Schwarz-Schilling, Grundig supervisory board</p>
<p>chairman, said the company would be able to survive on its own</p>
<p>and predicted it would return to profitability, but did not</p>
<p>elaborate.</p>
</text>
